        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "37a7c42e-0761-5132-a3d4-9b7380eef4b7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: none\n- Organizations: United States Coast Guard, United States, Soviet Union\n- Products: USS Barataria, USCGC Barataria\n- Events: Cuban Missile Crisis, Vietnam War\n- Places: Cuba, Italy, Turkey\n\nFacts:\n- From 1949 to 1969, USS Barataria (AVP-33) served in the United States Coast Guard as the cutter USCGC Barataria, designated WAVP-381 and later WHEC-381.\n- During her Coast Guard career, USCGC Barataria served in both the Cuban Missile Crisis and the Vietnam War.\n- The Cuban Missile Crisis was a 13-day confrontation from October 16 to October 28, 1962 between the United States and the Soviet Union.\n- The Cuban Missile Crisis concerned American ballistic missile deployments in Italy and Turkey and the consequent Soviet ballistic missile deployment in Cuba.\n- The Cuban Missile Crisis was also known as the October Crisis, the Caribbean Crisis, and the Missile Scare.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "83a50ce4-2958-5565-8c19-39ad180c7bad",
        "text": "Page: USS Barataria (AVP-33). Sentence: She then was transferred to the United States Coast Guard and was in commission as the Coast Guard cutter USCGC \"Barataria\" (WAVP-381), later WHEC-381 from 1949 to 1969, serving in the Cuban Missile Crisis and the Vietnam War during her lengthy Coast Guard career.\nPage: Cuban Missile Crisis. Sentence: The Cuban Missile Crisis, also known as the October Crisis (Spanish: \"Crisis de Octubre\" ), the Caribbean Crisis (Russian: Карибский кризис , \"Karibskij krizis\"), or the Missile Scare, was a 13-day (October 16–28, 1962) confrontation between the United States and the Soviet Union concerning American ballistic missile deployment in Italy and Turkey with consequent Soviet ballistic missile deployment in Cuba.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
